      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0101",
      "sequence": 113,
      "meaning": "The great sages conduct every marriage rite exactly as the Vedas prescribe. Holding sacred kuśa and his daughter’s hand, the mountain lord offers Bhavānī to Bhava. When Maheśa accepts her hand, every god’s heart rejoices; eminent sages recite Vedic mantras while the gods repeatedly hail Śaṅkara. Varied instruments sound and many kinds of flowers rain from the sky. Hara and Girijā are married, filling every world with celebration. Himālaya gives an indescribable dowry: maidservants and men, horses, chariots, elephants, cows, garments, jewels and many goods, with food packed in golden vessels.",
