    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0102",
      "sequence": 114,
      "meaning": "Śambhu consoles his mother-in-law in many ways; she bows at his feet and goes home. Umā’s mother summons her, takes her into her lap and lovingly teaches her always to worship Śaṅkara’s feet, for a wife’s dharma recognizes no second deity besides her husband. Tears fill her eyes as she speaks and embraces the maiden again. Lamenting how women were created in the world, she says a dependent person has no happiness even in a dream. Overwhelmed by love, the mother composes herself because the moment is unsuitable. She repeatedly meets Umā and falls clasping her feet; Bhavānī meets all the women, then returns and clings once more to her mother’s breast.",
