    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0103",
      "sequence": 115,
      "meaning": "The mountain king promptly returns, summons every mountain and lake, and dismisses each with honor, gifts, entreaty and esteem. When Śambhu reaches Kailāsa, all the gods return to their respective worlds. Śambhu and Bhavānī are the world’s mother and father, so the poet does not describe their intimate adornment. They enjoy varied delights and live on Kailāsa with the attendants; Hara and Girijā’s pastimes are ever new and much time passes. Then the six-faced prince is born and kills the demon Tāraka in battle. Āgamas, Vedas and Purāṇas proclaim it; Ṣaṇmukha’s birth is known throughout the world.",
