    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0104",
      "sequence": 116,
      "meaning": "Hearing Śambhu’s delightful, moving story, Bharadvāja feels immense joy and longing for more; tears fill his eyes and his hair stands erect. Love leaves him speechless. Seeing this, the wise sage rejoices and calls Bharadvāja’s birth blessed, for Gaurīśa is dear to him as life. Those without love for Śiva’s lotus feet do not please Rāma even in dreams; guileless love for Viśvanātha’s feet is a mark of Rāma’s devotee. Who equals Śiva in fidelity to Raghupati? Though Satī was faultless, he renounced marital relation with her and fulfilled his vow, thereby displaying devotion to Raghupati. Who is as dear to Rāma as Śiva? The narrator says he first asked about Śiva’s story to discern Bharadvāja’s heart and now knows him to be Rāma’s pure, faultless servant.",
